Month = {MAR},
Abstract = {This paper focuses on the physical attributes of land that intrinsically
   limit land use and possibly affect land values. In particular, we
   investigate if the slope of a land does decrease its price and
   investigate the role of land slope in forming more reliable
   constant-quality land price indices and aggregate house price indices.
   We find that, while land slopes do decrease the land price per unit,
   they have a small effect on the quality-adjusted land price indices in
   selected neighborhoods in Auckland, New Zealand, where sloped terrain is
   common.},
